  "note": "Step 7 speculative fixture (derivation A): every expect is derived by hand from the 60-wire topology and the p.86 rule (SHIFT LEFT ONE BIT whenever the rotary switch dial is turned), not printed: pp.86-87 print no lamp pattern, no pushbutton-to-light tie and no turn direction (O-C18). No erratum touches pp.86-87, so wires = as_printed. Topology: pushbutton n sets and latches relay n (nH-nG self-hold, output lamp n across nA/nB); wiper D16 on +, pad Dk on relay k's set-2 arm kL copies relay k into relay k-1 (K side puts + on (k-1)F for a 1, N side puts + on (k-1)E for a 0), D7 = 6E clears relay 6, D1 is a no-op (1K, 1N unwired), so bit 1 is dropped. Script choices, not printed: the entered number 101101 (pushbuttons 1, 3, 4, 6), clockwise turning one pad per 400 ms D1..D15 back to D0, and a dialRelease plus 1000 ms rest on D0 before each assert (Step 7 notes: never an until on a pass-through). The three revolutions cover every copy case: 1 onto 0, 0 onto 1, 1 onto 1 and 0 onto 0. Hardware-fragility note (O-C11, not asserted): each 0-copy makes the target relay buzz through its output lamp during the pad dwell; the settled 0 relies on the relay being out when the wiper breaks. Digest is a placeholder for the runner.",
